# What the build context does not need (step `mailer/1.21-container`).
#
# `target/` is the one that matters: it is hundreds of megabytes of the *host's* build output, and
# sending it to the daemon on every `podman build` is the difference between a build that starts
# immediately and one that spends a minute copying files nothing will use. The container builds its
# own release artifacts from source.
target/
.git/
.kiln/
tests/
mailer.toml
